  "narrative": "All new estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For the negative-direction SMARCA4 and PTEN claims, a positive signed estimate therefore means the exposed loss group has a lower dependency_composite score, i.e. stronger measured dependency, than the comparator. H79-H82 show that the SMARCA4-loss association is highly robust across TP53 and KEAP1 strata: signed contrasts are +0.833, +0.763, +0.796, and +0.814, with all 95% intervals entirely far above the 0.15-unit threshold. I therefore accept these as dataset-specific conditional associations and close these stratified main-effect investigations because the marginal SMARCA4 effect is already independently validated and the strata do not suggest a qualitative reversal. H89-H92 similarly show that the positive KEAP1-loss and TP53-loss associations remain robust within SMARCA4-loss and SMARCA4-nonloss strata: signed contrasts are +0.790, +0.809, +0.897, and +0.828, all well above threshold. These are accepted and closed as robustness checks of the already validated central associations. The PTEN-loss line is more nuanced. The marginal reversal H78 remains borderline overall, but H83, H87, and H88 provide threshold-level conditional support: signed contrasts are +0.259 within TP53-nonloss cells, +0.250 within KEAP1-nonloss cells, and +0.365 within KEAP1-loss cells, with lower bounds above 0.15. H84 within TP53-loss cells is only +0.160 with an interval crossing zero and threshold, likely because that cell is small. I keep H83, H87, and H88 accepted but active, and H84 unresolved active because the PTEN pattern may be smaller or less stable in TP53-loss contexts and still needs assessment in SMARCA4 strata and interaction tests. Multiplicity is a concern because this is a broad predictor screen, but the SMARCA4 and KEAP1/TP53 stratification effects are large relative to the threshold, whereas PTEN effects are smaller and thus I request independent validation for the central reversed PTEN claim H78 rather than relying only on conditional discovery evidence.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted central dataset associations: H6 KEAP1 loss -> higher dependency_composite, validated; H13 TP53 loss -> higher dependency_composite, validated; H77 SMARCA4 loss -> lower dependency_composite/stronger dependency, validated. H17 TP53 loss -> higher composite within KEAP1-loss cells, validated. New robust accepted conditionals closed: H79-H82 SMARCA4 loss lower scores across TP53/KEAP1 strata; H89-H92 KEAP1/TP53 positive effects across SMARCA4 strata. PTEN loss: H78 overall still unresolved (R33 0.239, CI 0.145-0.332), now requested validation. Accepted active PTEN conditionals: H83 TP53-nonloss (0.259, 0.169-0.349), H87 KEAP1-nonloss (0.250, 0.156-0.345), H88 KEAP1-loss (0.365, 0.180-0.550). H84 TP53-loss unresolved active (0.160, -0.023-0.344). Next informative PTEN follow-ups: H93/H94 within SMARCA4 strata, H98 PTEN-by-SMARCA4 interaction, H86/H100 triple strata if needed, and formal interactions H95-H97. Existing central effects and SMARCA4/KEAP1/TP53 conditionals can be considered sufficiently established for this supplied dataset; PTEN remains the main unresolved smaller predictor. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable.",
